        "locator": "body/sec[7]/sec[1]/sec[6]/sec[1]/p[6]",
        "population_status": "adult_dev_candidate",
        "section": "4 Therapy of chronic tinnitus / 4.1 Presentation of therapies with recommendations / 4.1.6 Pharmacological treatment / Evidence-based recommendation",
        "start": 0,
        "text": "Treatment of acute tinnitus follows the treatment recommendations for acute sudden hearing loss. For the treatment of acute hearing loss, corresponding guidelines (AWMF 017/2914 currently being updated [82]; guideline USA [83]) recommend systemic or intratympanic steroid treatment with, however, moderate evidence. Therefore, acute tinnitus with hearing loss or following hearing loss should be treated appropriately. If the tinnitus occurs acutely without measurable hearing loss, the standard cortisone therapy recommended for hearing loss is not recommended.",
        "chunk_id": "61d8c80cb5ed39d0375201d1",
        "document_id": "tinnitus-s3-2022",
        "version_id": "d5005279-1bad-491f-8122-a2d05e558146",
